.TH MERGEFOLDERS 1 "2026-11-01" "mergefolders 1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mergefolders \- merge sibling folders sharing a name prefix or suffix
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mergefolders.py
[\fB\-hvnolu\fR] {\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-e\fR} \fIN\fR
.br
.B mergefolders.py
\fB\-\-undo\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Groups the folders in the current directory by the first (\fB\-b\fR) or last
(\fB\-e\fR) \fIN\fR characters of their names. In every group of two or more,
the folder with the shortest name (ties broken alphabetically) becomes the
target and the files of the other folders are moved into it. Folders are never
deleted.
.PP
If a file of the same name exists in the target, the incoming file is renamed
\fIname_01.ext\fR, \fIname_02.ext\fR, ... unless \fB\-\-overwrite\fR is given.
.PP
With \fIN\fR = 0, all files from all subfolders (recursively) are moved into the
current directory instead.
.PP
All options are case-insensitive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-begin " " \fIN\fR
Group by the first \fIN\fR characters.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-end " " \fIN\fR
Group by the last \fIN\fR characters. Mutually exclusive with \fB\-b\fR.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target " " \fIDIR\fR
Instead of merging into the shortest-named folder, move the files of every
group into \fIDIR\fR/\fIkey\fR, where \fIkey\fR is the shared characters. The
folder is created if needed. With \fIN\fR = 0 all files go directly into \fIDIR\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print what would be done without changing anything.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-overwrite
Replace existing files on collision. Replaced files cannot be restored by undo.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log
Append all actions to \fIlog.txt\fR.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-undo
Reverse the last run using \fIundo_merge.json\fR, which is removed on success.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I undo_merge.json
Written after each run that moved files; read by \fB\-\-undo\fR.
.TP
.I log.txt
Appended to when \fB\-\-log\fR is used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if an error occurred or files were skipped, 2 for invalid usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mergefolders.py \-\-dry\-run \-b 8
mergefolders.py \-b 8 \-l
mergefolders.py \-e 4 \-\-overwrite
mergefolders.py \-t condensed \-b 5
mergefolders.py \-u
.fi
